# n8n automation credential, classified by service.
#
# Install as /etc/facai-cloud/providers/n8n.env, owned by root:facai with mode
# 0640:
#   install -d -m 0750 -o root -g facai /etc/facai-cloud/providers
#   install -m 0640 -o root -g facai n8n.env.example /etc/facai-cloud/providers/n8n.env
# Then edit it and fill in the real values. NEVER commit this file with values.
#
# Facai reads these by name from the process environment and never prints or
# returns their values. The n8n webhook URL itself is treated as a secret (the
# path usually contains an unguessable id) and is never shown in the console.
# Until BOTH values are present the integration reports CONFIG_REQUIRED, sends
# nothing and never claims to be connected.
#
# n8n Webhook URL (Production webhook, receives Facai mission/stage events).
N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Shared secret used as the HMAC-SHA256 key for outbound signing and inbound
# callback verification. Use a long random value; the same value is configured
# in the n8n workflow.
N8N_SIGNING_SECRET=
# Optional tuning. Leave empty to use the defaults shown.
# N8N_TIMEOUT=15
# N8N_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# N8N_MAX_SKEW=300
